    "issue": {
      "shortcode": "SCT-1000",
      "title": "Secrets detected in source code",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "category": "SECRETS",
      "shortDescription": "Secrets should never be checked into source code. Ideally, they should be injected into the runtime and then the values should be picked from there.",
      "description": "Secrets should never be checked into source code. Ideally, they should be injected into the runtime and then the values should be picked from there.\n\n<!--more-->\n\nExamples of secrets are SSH keys, API keys and secrets (AWS or Stripe APIs, for example), database credentials etc.\n\n### Bad practice\nIn the sample Python code below, the secrets have been hardcoded:\n\n```python\nkey = \"12345azan+/ryGUuk\"\n```\n\n### Recommended\nIdeally, this should be picked from the environment, like:\n\n```python\nkey = os.getenv(\"SECRET_KEY\")\n```",
      "tags": [],
      "autofixAvailable": false,
      "autofixAiAvailable": false,
      "isRecommended": false
    },
