    "repositoryIssueId": "UmVwb3NpdG9yeUlzc3VlOm92eXhyYXk=",
    "issue": {
      "shortcode": "SCT-1004",
      "title": "Hardcoded JavaScript Web Token in source code",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "category": "SECRETS",
      "shortDescription": "Leaking a JavaScript Web Token (JWT) in the source code can pose a serious security risk, as it can give unauthorized access to resources and sensitive information in the web application. This can lead to data breaches and loss of confidential information.\n\nIf a JWT secret has been leaked, you can deprecate the old secret and use a new one to mitigate the vulnerability.",
      "description": "Leaking a JavaScript Web Token (JWT) in the source code can pose a serious security risk, as it can give unauthorized access to resources and sensitive information in the web application. This can lead to data breaches and loss of confidential information.\n\nIf a JWT secret has been leaked, you can deprecate the old secret and use a new one to mitigate the vulnerability.\n\n<!--more-->\n\nIt is recommended to remove any hard-coded secrets from source code and instead use environment variables or a secure key management service (KMS) to store and manage secrets. Additionally, it is important to ensure that only authorized users have access to these secrets.\n\n### Bad practice\n\n```javascript\nconst jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');\n\nconst user = {\n  id: 1,\n  username: 'john.doe',\n  role: 'admin'\n};\n\nconst token = jwt.sign(user, 'SUPER_CONFIDENTIAL_SECRET');\n```\n\n### Recommended\n\n```javascript\nconst jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');\nconst dotenv = require('dotenv');\n\ndotenv.config(); // loads environment variables from a .env file\n\nconst user = {\n  id: 1,\n  username: 'john.doe',\n  role: 'admin'\n};\n\nconst token = jwt.sign(user, process.env.JWT_SECRET);\n```",
      "tags": [],
      "autofixAvailable": false,
      "autofixAiAvailable": false,
      "isRecommended": false
    },
