      "shortcode": "SCT-A000",
      "title": "Possible hardcoded secrets detected in source code",
      "severity": "MINOR",
      "category": "SECRETS",
      "shortDescription": "Hardcoded secret with a low Shannon entropy (<4.5) detected in source code. This could be a valid secret and it is recommended to audit the use and verify if it is indeed valid.",
      "description": "Hardcoded secret with a low Shannon entropy (<4.5) detected in source code.\nThis could be a valid secret and it is recommended to audit the use and verify if it is indeed valid.\n\nIf it is a place-holder, you can ignore this issue, or add a `skipcq: SCT-A000` pragma to [silence this warning](https://docs.deepsource.com/docs/issues-ignore-rules#silencing-a-specific-issue).\n\nThis issue is detected for secrets that are assigned to a variable having `password`, `secret` and `_key` in their name,\nand the value of the secret has a Shannon entropy between 3 and 4.5.",
      "tags": [],
      "autofixAvailable": false,
      "autofixAiAvailable": false,
      "isRecommended": false
    },
